<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Guise</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Guise was a French ducal family, a junior branch of the House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> founded by Claude of Lorraine, who was made Duke of Guise in 1528. Its leaders, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-duke-of-guise">Francis, Duke of Guise</a>, and his son Henry, headed the Catholic party and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a>. The main line died out in 1675.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-guise.jpg" alt="House of Guise" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Claude_de_Lorraine_(2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
